Startrek instructions (just to get you started)

The enterprise looks like «ê∂
A starbase looks like Æ Ø
A Klingon looks like a Happy face prefixed and suffixed by +
(I can't figure out how to get a Happy face within the editor)
The function keys give the possible actions:

F1 - NAV - navigate: move somewhere.  Course and speed must be given.
F2 - SRS - Short range scan
F3 - LRS - Long Range Scan: adjacent quadrants.  Of the nine shown,
           you are always in the middle.
F4 - PHA - Fire phasers.  Will be prompted for energy units to fire.
F5 - TOR - Fire Photon Torpedos.  Prompt for direction.
F6 - SHI - Transfer energy to shields.  Prompt for energy amount
F7 - DAM - Damage control report.  Status of all systems.
F8 - COM - Library computer functions.  Will give you a new function
           key line (discussed below)
F9 - RES - Resign

Computer functions

F1 - GAL - Cumulative record for whole galaxy.  8 x 8 quadrants.
           Gives information only if you've visited or scanned
           that quadrant.
F2 - STA - Status report, number of klingons left, damage state.
F3 - TOR - Torpedo data.  Calculates direction and distance of Klingon.
           Reliable only if direction is a whole number (needs work)
F4 - BAS - Starbase navigation data:  Direction & distance to starbase.
           Has same problems as TOR.
F5 - DIR/DIS - Direction and distance calculator.  Again not to
F6 - REGION NAME MAP - Gives you names of quadrants, just in case you care.

Directional coordinate system:  I may not draw this well, but draw
an intersecting horizontal and vertical line.  Directions are as follows
1 - Straight right
2 - Halfway between vertical and right
3 - Straight up
4 - Halfway between vertical and left
5 - Straight left
6 - Halfway between left and down
7 - Straight down
8 - Halfway between down and right
9 - Supposed to be synonymous with 1, but I'm not sure it works.

Speed may be fractional.  Decimal speed of 0.1 moves one sector.
Speed of 1 moves 1 quadrant.

Within the LRS and SRS displays, a three digit number is displayed.
Interpret it as:

      KBS    

Where K=number of Klingons left in that quadrant
      B=number of Starbases in that quadrant
      S=number of stars in that quadrant


This program is distributed "AS IS".  It certainly needs work, but
at least we're started off.

